$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 67-66-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.3. Synthesis of Mono-ols and Monoacids.
3.3.1. Synthesis of Monoacids. To a solution of 1 mmol mono-ols and 1.2
mmol diacid (1,18-octadec-9-enedioic acid) in 10 mL of CHCl3 under the
protection of N2, 0.4 mmol DMAP was added, followed by 1.1 mmol DCC. The
reaction was carried out at room temperature overnight. The precipitated
dicyclohexylurea was removed by filtration. The organic phase was diluted
with 10 mL of chloroform then washed sequentially with water (3 x 20 mL),
4% aqueous NaHCO3 (2 x 200 mL), and brine (3 x 200 mL), and then dried
over Na2SO4. After filtration, the filtrate was concentrated with a
rotary evaporator and the residue was purified by column chromatography
with ethyl acetate and hexanes as the eluent. From
2-hydroxypropane-1,3-diyl dioleate and 1,18-Octadec-9-enedioic acid. From
mono-ol 2 and 1,18-octadec-9-enedioic acid. Monoacid 3, yield 71%. 1H-NMR
(in CDCl3, δ/ ppm): 5.35-5.30 (14H,m), 5.24-5.22 (3H,m), 4.28-4.24 (6H,
m), 4.14-4.09 (6H,m), 2.33-2.26(20H, m), 2.00-1.93(28H, m), 1.59-1.56
(20H, m), 1.36-1.24 (128H,m), 0.87-0.83 (12H, t).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, acid reactant concentration dependent product formation,
Steglich esterification
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Physical Properties of Triacylglycerol Oligomers: Examining
the Physical Functionality Potential of Self-Metathesized Highly
Unsaturated Vegetable Oils
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Shaojun; Bouzidi, Laziz; Narine, Suresh S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research (2013), 52(6), 2209-2219

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME393 STEP1
